{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-141286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979886/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1636787db7fdb01bff7888c0b2ae15149f23f3ea5c4491b24ffba985fae3980"} {"question" "q-141286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979886/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1636787db7fdb01bff7888c0b2ae15149f23f3ea5c4491b24ffba985fae3980"} {"question" "q-141286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979886/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6980450903c1aa78562080ae506961f662f89a759004cadf4351f0ee99276815"} {"question" "q-141286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/q